From 4d8e5b5316d83f8683bebce8956c27533b0d8aee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:59:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] arm64: dts: apple: Add the J775D (Mac Studio, M5 Ultra)
 device trees

Add the T6050 SoC in its two-die M5 Ultra form, and the Mac Studio board
that uses it: the device tree for Linux running on the hardware, as the
boot loader hands it over (the loader fills the tunables and calibration
the nodes name).

Every T6050 is made of the same die, so the SoC description is split as
for the M3 Max and Ultra (t6031-base, -die0, -dieX):

- t6050-base.dtsi: the nodes common to every size, die 0's bus and the
  CPU node template;
- t6050-die0.dtsi: the blocks used on die 0 only, among them the
  interrupt controller that serves both dies;
- t6050-dieX.dtsi: the per-die template, included once for each die,
  with each die's blocks at the die stride and its interrupts on its
  own die of the AIC;
- t6050-ultra.dtsi: the two dies, their CPUs (five cores in each
  cluster) and the blocks so far described for the two-die part only:
  the video decoders, the memory cache controllers, the display
  subsystem, die 1's ATC0 and its DisplayPort PHY;
- t6050-j775d.dts: the board, its USB-C ports and their PD controllers,
  the HDMI port, PCIe, audio, the boot NOR and the fans.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
[erik: dropped references to private files from a comment]
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
